1413	Undergraduate 2026-2027	ENTR 1511	ENTR	1511	The Entrepreneurial Mindset	Entrepreneurship	Designed to help students understand what an entrepreneurial mindset is and guide them in developing their own entrepreneurial mindset. An entrepreneurial mindset manifests as an inclination to discover, evaluate, and exploit opportunities, to passionately seek out new opportunities, to pursue opportunities with discipline, to anchor on the right opportunities, to focus on the execution of opportunities, and to engage others to support one’s mindset and actions. These opportunities exist everywhere, whether as a potential for a newly engineered solution to a medical need, leveraging of digital technologies in novel ways to address social needs, innovating public policies to more effectively allocate resources in society, or facilitating new ways for individuals to communicate or otherwise engage. An entrepreneurial mindset is rooted in specific entrepreneurial principles that drive key behaviors (e.g., prototyping, experimentation, storytelling) to help individuals more effectively recognize and take advantage of opportunities. Students will gain an appreciation of the principles that underpin an entrepreneurial mindset and enact the principles in a series of experiential exercises.	3	3	(3)	\N	\N	\N
1414	Undergraduate 2026-2027	ENTR 3000	ENTR	3000	Special Topics - Entrepreneurship	Entrepreneurship	Serves as a special topics course for the undergraduate certificate in entrepreneurship.	3	3	(3)	\N	\N	\N
1415	Undergraduate 2026-2027	ENTR 3276	ENTR	3276	Recognizing Entrepreneurial Opportunities	Entrepreneurship	Helps students take the first step as an entrepreneur. Before entrepreneurs can organize ventures around innovative solutions to exploit opportunities, entrepreneurs benefit from first recognizing and evaluating opportunities. Students achieve two course objectives fundamental to being an entrepreneur: (1) students put together an opportunity portfolio - a detailed understanding and analysis of an industry/technology and all of the situational conditions that inform the opportunity within that industry/technology context; and (2) based on this opportunity portfolio, students are tasked with pitching a potential solution to a specific opportunity.	3	3	(3)	\N	\N	\N
1416	Undergraduate 2026-2027	ENTR 3278	ENTR	3278	Experiential Entrepreneurship	Entrepreneurship	Entrepreneurs work in contexts where they cannot control what ultimately occurs. As means to increase students’ self-confidence and mental fortitude for uncertain contexts, this course seeks to present students with conditions of uncertainty and complexity. It involves different approaches, from engaged learning exercises, individual and team projects, to interactions with entrepreneurs.	3	3	(3)	\N	\N	\N
1417	Undergraduate 2026-2027	ENTR 3279	ENTR	3279	Entrepreneurial Action and Organizing	Entrepreneurship	Many individuals often recognize the same opportunities, but only some individuals become entrepreneurs by taking the actions to exploit the opportunity, and only a few of the entrepreneurs become successful by exploiting the opportunity effectively. This course provides students with an understanding of how they can shift from recognizing opportunities to taking actions to exploit the opportunities to create value for a market and for society. It involves a combination of readings, casework, and experiential exercises aimed at helping students learn from real entrepreneurs’ experiences, but also providing initial exercises to allow students to put into action what they have learned.	3	3	(3)	\N	\N	\N
