1864	Undergraduate 2026-2027	HIST 3171	HIST	3171	Comparative Genocide	History	The term “genocide” is often used imprecisely in popular and political discourse. Through examinations of several case studies - the Armenian genocide, the Holocaust, and post-war genocides in Cambodia, Guatemala, and Rwanda, among others - this course explores the roots and the psychological, cultural, and political impacts of genocide and other forms of mass violence.	3	3	(3)	\N	\N	\N
