1886	Undergraduate 2026-2027	HIST 3272	HIST	3272	The History of Disney, 1923-2004	History	One might be hard pressed to name a business with a more diversified portfolio than The Walt Disney Company, from its early and humble beginnings (that actually started in a garage) to a corporation that has an extraordinary global position in entertainment and leisure. Disney is synonymous with family-oriented entertainment, a perception it rigorously and litigiously defends, but which critics consistently argue saccharinized history, society, culture, and reality. It has always been a company that encourages and inspires innovation and technology, yet is grounded firmly in a nostalgic sense of Americana. It adopts old world tales and myths, but uses new technology to retell and reimagine them. This course is designed to explore these often contradictory, and equally often complimentary, elements of the man and the company, because few companies or corporations are still so readily identified with a single person more than fifty years after its founder’s death. Disney is a cultural, economic, and technology driven company, a product of twentieth-century America, all of which are a part of this course.	3	3	(3)	\N	\N	\N
