128	course	ANTH 2126	ANTH 2126 World Population Problems An examination of various world population “problems,” such as growth, migration, fertility, and population aging, in order to learn how cultural, political, economic, and environmental factors influence and are influenced by the population structure of a given society.	{"code": "ANTH 2126", "catalog": "Undergraduate 2026-2027"}	\N
129	course	ANTH 2127	ANTH 2127 Environmental Anthropology Anthropological approaches to environmental issues as they affect people around the world, including the relationships between humans and their natural environments, cultural knowledge about environments, the role of wealth and inequality in environmental interactions, international and global environmental governance, and the effects of these on management decisions and outcomes.	{"code": "ANTH 2127", "catalog": "Undergraduate 2026-2027"}	\N
