380	course	BINF 1101	BINF 1101 Introduction to Bioinformatics and Genomics Introduction to the genomics perspective in the life sciences, combining a general introduction to genomic technologies and the bioinformatics methods used to analyze genome-scale data with a presentation of real world scientific problems where these technologies are having an impact. The lab component provides hands-on experience with biological sequence and structure databases, using small-scale projects to introduce students to the world of bioinformatics research.	{"code": "BINF 1101", "catalog": "Undergraduate 2026-2027"}	\N
