459	course	BIOL 4242L	BIOL 4242L Biology of Birds Laboratory The laboratory and field portion of the Biology of Birds focuses on field identification and inventory techniques, with an introduction to anatomy. Binoculars are required. Meets for one three-hour period per week.	{"code": "BIOL 4242L", "catalog": "Undergraduate 2026-2027"}	\N
460	course	BIOL 4243	BIOL 4243 Animal Behavior An ethological approach to how animals respond to their environment. Causation, development, and adaptive significance of behavior in social systems.	{"code": "BIOL 4243", "catalog": "Undergraduate 2026-2027"}	\N
