933	course	DANC 3231	DANC 3231 Choreography in Context: Danced Collaborations in Urban Spaces Examines ways in which we can make art in the context of our physical environments, audiences, and communities, specifically through the processes of site-specific work and community collaborations. The practice of improvisation as a process and product for making dance and performance are deeply investigated. Drawing on the history and methodologies of improvisation, site-specific, and community-centered artists, students build a foundation for and develop their creative skill sets as they improvise, make, and perform dances outside the traditional theatre space.	{"code": "DANC 3231", "catalog": "Undergraduate 2026-2027"}	\N
