934	course	DANC 3232	DANC 3232 Digital Skills for Artists An interdisciplinary course that provides students with the tools to work with digital design and marketing, visual communications, sound editing, and video production. Students learn the basics of effective visual communications, produce visual content and learn to edit videos and photos for online viewing, and become versed in the fundamentals of sound creation and editing. The course culminates in the production of a professional website using digital skills and media tools practiced throughout the semester.	{"code": "DANC 3232", "catalog": "Undergraduate 2026-2027"}	\N
