972	course	ECEI 2111	ECEI 2111 Theoretical Foundations of Early Childhood Care and Education A rigorous overview of the history of early childhood education (ECE), early intervention/early childhood special education (EI/ECSE), and the broader field of child and family studies. Coursework will focus on history, philosophy, theories of child development across domains, professional roles and responsibilities, best practices, contemporary issues, pertinent legislation, and the range of settings and environments in which professionals and families collaborate to achieve positive outcomes for young children and their families.	{"code": "ECEI 2111", "catalog": "Undergraduate 2026-2027"}	\N
