975	course	ECEI 2412	ECEI 2412 Clinical I: Applied Early Learning in Childhood Settings Effective methods of observation, documentation, and assessment as related to developmental theory for young children age Birth-5. This course will also include virtual seminars where candidates will meet with the course instructor to learn about conducting observations of young children and debrief their observations from the field.	{"code": "ECEI 2412", "catalog": "Undergraduate 2026-2027"}	\N
976	course	ECEI 3112	ECEI 3112 Supporting Young Learners - Birth through Kindergarten: Introductory Methods Focuses on children’s developmental and individual needs, curriculum decisions, and the design of early learning environments. This course explores topics such as curricula models and frameworks, professional roles, application of developmental domains and academic disciplines, curricula implementation, and provides an introduction to assessment and progress monitoring. A corresponding clinical will be required.	{"code": "ECEI 3112", "catalog": "Undergraduate 2026-2027"}	\N
977	course	ECEI 3114	ECEI 3114 Advanced Infant-Toddler Methods 0-3 Provides opportunities to examine early childhood learning environments and integrated approaches to supporting young children aged 0-2 years of all ability levels with an emphasis on practice in applied settings. Specifically, in this course students learn naturalistic and instructional strategies that support children’s active learning across developmental domains (including play) in a range of routines and activities. This course also emphasizes the importance of transitions and relationships to support children’s learning.	{"code": "ECEI 3114", "catalog": "Undergraduate 2026-2027"}	\N
978	course	ECEI 3210	ECEI 3210 Enhancing the Social-Emotional Development of Young Children in Inclusive Settings This course will review and analyze the social-emotional development and behaviors of young children, birth through kindergarten, in all early childhood settings. This course will explore young children’s social-emotional development; the effects of potential risk factors and disability (e.g., neurodiversity, communication delays) on social-emotional development related to ecological influences; evidence-based practices to support social and emotional growth and learning, including tiered behavioral supports, behavior support plans, and implementation efforts. Students learn how to conduct functional behavior assessments, prevent and respond to challenging behaviors, and build social competence in young children in a variety of early childhood settings. A corresponding clinical (ECEI 2412 ) will be required.	{"code": "ECEI 3210", "catalog": "Undergraduate 2026-2027"}	\N
979	course	ECEI 3412	ECEI 3412 Clinical II: Applied Learning in Early Childhood Settings Practical application of advanced methods of designing, implementing, and assessing learning experiences in support of children’s development (birth through 5 years). A community-based clinical assignment is required where each candidate will engage in various community settings. Additionally, a seminar experience will be required where candidates will engage in peer collaboration and learning across experiences and coursework. The courses associated with this clinical are ECEI 3114 , ECEI 4114 , and ECEI 4112 .	{"code": "ECEI 3412", "catalog": "Undergraduate 2026-2027"}	\N
