1001	course	ESCI 3190	ESCI 3190 Biogeography The patterns of life across the Earth and the causes of those patterns, with an emphasis on ecological patterns and historical patterns of biodiversity. The origin of the Earth’s biological diversity and methods for conserving that biodiversity is also discussed. Emphasis on student oral and written communication.	{"code": "ESCI 3190", "catalog": "Undergraduate 2026-2027"}	\N
