1554	course	ETFS 3103	ETFS 3103 Fire Behavior Explores the theories and fundamentals of how and why fires start, spread, and are controlled. Topics include: basic principles of heat transfer, ignition of liquids and solids; fire growth and spread, compartment fire temperatures, and compartment fire phenomena.	{"code": "ETFS 3103", "catalog": "Undergraduate 2026-2027"}	\N
