1705	course	GEOL 4105	GEOL 4105 Geomorphology Discusses surficial processes and landform development as controlled by climate, tectonics, rock characteristics and time. An emphasis is placed on field-based analyses of weathering, erosion, mass wasting (landslides and rock falls), and surface water processes (flooding and floodplains), and how climate change and tectonics may affect them in landscape development.	{"code": "GEOL 4105", "catalog": "Undergraduate 2026-2027"}	\N
