1718	course	GRNT 2100	GRNT 2100 Aging and the Lifecourse An interdisciplinary course that examines the phenomenon of aging and its consequences for society from a variety of perspectives. Students participate in lectures, discussions and service learning projects designed to give them a broad overview of the field of gerontology. Emphasis on the wide variation in the aging process and approaches to meeting the needs of the aging population.	{"code": "GRNT 2100", "catalog": "Undergraduate 2026-2027"}	\N
