1727	course	GRNT 4110	GRNT 4110 Sociology of Aging Changing characteristics, aspirations and needs of older adults and their impact upon such institutions as the family, work, the economy, politics, education and healthcare; emphasis on sociological theories of aging, contemporary research, and the analysis of specific aging policies and programs.	{"code": "GRNT 4110", "catalog": "Undergraduate 2026-2027"}	\N
