1938	course	GLST 2112	GLST 2112 Problems in Globalization An examination of the paradoxes of contemporary globalization. Through lectures, discussions, and student presentations, we study the cultural, economic, social and political impact of globalization. We explore how scholars have defined globalization and consider the mechanisms and agents of change. We examine different forms of global governance and if there is an emerging global culture. Finally, we investigate how the international community addresses problems such as poverty, refugee resettlement, immigration, human trafficking, terrorism, and climate change.	{"code": "GLST 2112", "catalog": "Undergraduate 2026-2027"}	\N
