2243	course	MATH 2164	MATH 2164 Matrices and Linear Algebra Matrix algebra, systems of linear equations, vector spaces, linear transformations, determinants, inner products, eigenvalues.	{"code": "MATH 2164", "catalog": "Undergraduate 2026-2027"}	\N
2244	course	MATH 2165	MATH 2165 Introduction to Discrete Structures Propositions and truth tables, sets, permutations and combinations, relations and functions, lattices, and trees.	{"code": "MATH 2165", "catalog": "Undergraduate 2026-2027"}	\N
2245	course	MATH 2167	MATH 2167 Introduction to Mathematical Reasoning Focuses on the fundamentals of logical reasoning and mathematical proof-writing. Students will learn what a proof is in mathematics, how to analyze a proof for validity, and have practice writing their simple proofs. Students will also be exposed to mathematical programs, such as LaTex, and learn how to typeset their proofs. Topics covered include symbolic logic (such as truth tables & quantifiers), types of proof-writing (such as direct proofs, proofs by contrapositive, proofs by contradiction, counter-examples, and mathematical induction), and other basic concepts from set theory, relations, and functions (such as bijections).	{"code": "MATH 2167", "catalog": "Undergraduate 2026-2027"}	\N
