2253	course	MATH 2688	MATH 2688 Mathematics Awareness Seminar This seminar focuses on the different areas of study and career opportunities within the mathematics, statistics, and mathematics education fields. Discussions in class and with visiting speakers include topics of internships, cooperative education, and job opportunities while still in school as well as after graduation discussions about career opportunities, resumes, cover letters, and strategies on interviewing with companies. There are also discussions about graduate school, the best fit graduate school based upon a student’s interests, how to apply, and GRE and GMAT possible requirements. Recommended to be taken during the Sophomore year.	{"code": "MATH 2688", "catalog": "Undergraduate 2026-2027"}	\N
