2428	course	MEGR 4281	MEGR 4281 GD&T for Design and Inspection Reconciles the engineering design process with manufacturing quality control. These two conceptual domains of geometric specification (from the perspective of a designer) and verification (from the perspective of a metrologist) are brought together in a comprehensive and integrated manner in this class. Students will learn to (i) develop and interpret rigorous engineering drawings, (ii) convey and recognize design intent via geometric specification, and (iii) anticipate and apply inspection and metrology techniques to verify that manufactured components meet specification. These goals will be met through the coverage of topics such as geometric dimensioning and tolerancing (GD&T), dimensional inspection techniques, and coordinate metrology. Recent developments and special topics will also be presented including model-based definition (MBD), digital twins, ‘Industry 4.0,’ novel metrology techniques, and advanced computational metrology.	{"code": "MEGR 4281", "catalog": "Undergraduate 2026-2027"}	\N
