2622	course	MUED 2200	MUED 2200 Foundations of Music Education Examination of the social, historical, legal, and philosophical foundations of music education, major issues in American education as they relate to music education research, classroom diversity issues, and instructional planning. Clinical experiences required.	{"code": "MUED 2200", "catalog": "Undergraduate 2026-2027"}	\N
2623	course	MUED 2241	MUED 2241 Music Development and Learning Introduction to human developmental learning theories and the psychology of music as they relate to teaching music in public schools. Topics include research-based perspectives of: 1) education developmental learning theories; 2) musical learning; 3) teaching musical skills; and 4) musical roles. Clinical experiences in various levels and music education settings (general music, band, choir, and/or orchestra) required.	{"code": "MUED 2241", "catalog": "Undergraduate 2026-2027"}	\N
2624	course	MUED 3101	MUED 3101 Technology for Music Educators Prepares future music teachers to effectively integrate technology into the K-12 music teaching and learning environment. Covers the standard applications of music technology, including general computing processes, digital audio, MIDI, music notation, and computer-aided instruction. Requirements include a project focused on music and culture outside of the classical music canon.	{"code": "MUED 3101", "catalog": "Undergraduate 2026-2027"}	\N
