3339	course	SOCY 3120	SOCY 3120 Examining Institutional Racism: Implications for Contemporary Leadership A collaborative effort among scholars and the professor to employ the Sociological approach to the investigation and understanding of institutional racism. Implications for emerging leaders and the employment of antiracist attitudes and actions are discussed. The concepts of institutional racism and antiracism are introduced, and then specific topics are reviewed throughout the term. In addition to deepening the knowledge and understanding that students gain and share, all are called to action at the end of the semester. The intellectual pursuit and generation of ideas should not be the end point, but the beginning of ideas and strategies for action.	{"code": "SOCY 3120", "catalog": "Undergraduate 2026-2027"}	\N
