3614	course	THEA 2600	THEA 2600 Majors Seminar Students investigate, identify, analyze, and cultivate immediate and life-long career options through directed projects, guest lectures, site visits to the Career Center, mock interviews, and other career preparatory activities and assignments. Students develop effective communication skills (both written and oral) as part of their work on the course projects. Two contact hours.	{"code": "THEA 2600", "catalog": "Undergraduate 2026-2027"}	\N
