3714	course	URBS 2200	URBS 2200 Introduction to Urban Studies A survey course exploring the diverse perspectives and experience of North American Cities. Lectures and discussions focus on the development, organization, function, and meaning of urban areas, as well as the multiple and complex relationships that exist between cities and the people who live and work within them.	{"code": "URBS 2200", "catalog": "Undergraduate 2026-2027"}	\N
