4353	occupation	35-2012.00	Cooks, Institution and Cafeteria Prepare and cook large quantities of food for institutions, such as schools, hospitals, or cafeterias.	{"soc_code": "35-2012.00"}	\N
4354	occupation	35-2013.00	Cooks, Private Household Prepare meals in private homes. Includes personal chefs.	{"soc_code": "35-2013.00"}	\N
4355	occupation	35-2014.00	Cooks, Restaurant Prepare, season, and cook dishes such as soups, meats, vegetables, or desserts in restaurants. May order supplies, keep records and accounts, price items on menu, or plan menu.	{"soc_code": "35-2014.00"}	\N
4356	occupation	35-2015.00	Cooks, Short Order Prepare and cook to order a variety of foods that require only a short preparation time. May take orders from customers and serve patrons at counters or tables.	{"soc_code": "35-2015.00"}	\N
4357	occupation	35-2019.00	Cooks, All Other All cooks not listed separately.	{"soc_code": "35-2019.00"}	\N
4358	occupation	35-2021.00	Food Preparation Workers Perform a variety of food preparation duties other than cooking, such as preparing cold foods and shellfish, slicing meat, and brewing coffee or tea.	{"soc_code": "35-2021.00"}	\N
4359	occupation	35-3011.00	Bartenders Mix and serve drinks to patrons, directly or through waitstaff.	{"soc_code": "35-3011.00"}	\N
4360	occupation	35-3023.00	Fast Food and Counter Workers Perform duties such as taking orders and serving food and beverages. Serve customers at counter or from a steam table. May take payment. May prepare food and beverages.	{"soc_code": "35-3023.00"}	\N
4361	occupation	35-3023.01	Baristas Prepare or serve specialty coffee or other beverages. Serve food such as baked goods or sandwiches to patrons.	{"soc_code": "35-3023.01"}	\N
4362	occupation	35-3031.00	Waiters and Waitresses Take orders and serve food and beverages to patrons at tables in dining establishment.	{"soc_code": "35-3031.00"}	\N
4363	occupation	35-3041.00	Food Servers, Nonrestaurant Serve food to individuals outside of a restaurant environment, such as in hotel rooms, hospital rooms, residential care facilities, or cars.	{"soc_code": "35-3041.00"}	\N
4364	occupation	35-9011.00	Dining Room and Cafeteria Attendants and Bartender Helpers Facilitate food service. Clean tables; remove dirty dishes; replace soiled table linens; set tables; replenish supply of clean linens, silverware, glassware, and dishes; supply service bar with food; and serve items such as water, condiments, and coffee to patrons.	{"soc_code": "35-9011.00"}	\N
4365	occupation	35-9021.00	Dishwashers Clean dishes, kitchen, food preparation equipment, or utensils.	{"soc_code": "35-9021.00"}	\N
4366	occupation	35-9031.00	Hosts and Hostesses, Restaurant, Lounge, and Coffee Shop Welcome patrons, seat them at tables or in lounge, and help ensure quality of facilities and service.	{"soc_code": "35-9031.00"}	\N
4367	occupation	35-9099.00	Food Preparation and Serving Related Workers, All Other All food preparation and serving related workers not listed separately.	{"soc_code": "35-9099.00"}	\N
